      "overall_rating": 0,
      "review_title": "",
      "review_description": "VI was prepared to provide an open book quote that showed how competitive this market is now.  6-7 years ago I was up for around $25,000.  Our system cost $10,000 for a very good 5.3kw system (German) and apayback of around 5 years although this is yet to be confirmed.  I'll need to due some heavy tree cutting pruning to boost performance.One thing that I did not pick was the massive rise is electricity prices from 1/7/12.  I am concerned the feed in tarrif of around 23 cent per KWH is only a fraction of my marginal cost of 40c pkwh.  This is further compounded by the fact that most of my power generation (day) will not match my peak use (night) so whilst I may end up carbon nuetral my electricity bill may not show the same result.  I'll be interested in reviewing it after a full year.",
